WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.090
In English, you can say 'the film I saw'.

2
00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:04.640
No 'that' needed.

3
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.450
Try that word for word in French,

4
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.260
and a French speaker would
stop you right there.

5
00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.830
French wants «le film que j'ai vu».

6
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:13.740
One extra word.

7
00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.160
And French doesn't have
just one linking word.

8
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.230
It has three to choose from.

9
00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.310
So why can't French leave out the 'that',

10
00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.750
when English drops it all the time?

11
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.900
In this mission, you'll
join two sentences into one,

12
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.500
with a single link.

13
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.970
Then you'll join pairs
yourself in the lab,

14
00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.380
and choose the right link each time.

15
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.790
Your mission: find out
why French keeps the link.
